# Demo Video Script — EnderAI (FastAPI App)

Created: 2026-02-03 09:14 UTC  
Last used: 2026-02-03 09:15 UTC

## Version
- Draft v0.2 (YC-focused walkthrough)

## Length Target
- 3–5 minutes

## Audience
- Y Combinator partners + early-stage operators evaluating leverage and execution velocity.

## Core Promise
- EnderAI turns messy work-in-motion into a tight, auditable ship loop and builds reusable memory so future workflows run faster with less user input.

## Demo Narrative (Beats)
1) **Hook: Founder Speed (0:00–0:30)**
   - “Teams lose days to missing tickets and stale boards. EnderAI closes those gaps automatically.”
   - Show FastAPI items UI + Kanban board side by side.

2) **Work in Motion (0:30–1:15)**
   - Show items list in the FastAPI app (real data).
   - Show the Kanban board with existing issues in flight.
   - Call out: “Everything is wired — GitHub Issues, board automation, repos, and deploys.”

3) **Memory in Action (1:15–2:00)**
   - Highlight “memory used” from prior tickets (known patterns, prior decisions, commands).
   - Note: “We don’t start from zero; EnderAI reuses proven context.”

4) **The Gap (2:00–3:00)**
   - Move a task on the board and notice missing frontend ticket for archived items UI.
   - Ask EnderAI to create it from context.
   - Show the issue appear in GitHub and auto‑land in the right column.

5) **Execution Loop (3:00–4:00)**
   - Open frontend repo, point to the created issue.
   - Mention auto‑deploys for frontend + backend.
   - Close the issue; show the board update.

6) **Trust + Auditability (4:00–4:40)**
   - Open today’s Flight Log and show the audit trail (requests → commands → outcomes).
   - Emphasize: “No guessing, no lost context. You can audit the work.”

7) **Wrap: Repeatable Outcomes (4:40–5:00)**
   - “EnderAI compresses coordination overhead into minutes and makes outcomes repeatable.”
   - “Memory used, memory created, and memory promoted → faster future workflows.”

## Shot List (Concrete Screens)
- FastAPI demo app (items list)
- GitHub Issues (frontend repo)
- Kanban board (issues auto‑added)
- Render deploys (frontend + backend)
- DB query output (items/users)
- Flight Log entry (today)

## Script (Talk Track)
- Hook: “Every team has the same problem: missing tickets and stale boards. EnderAI closes those gaps automatically.”
- Setup: “We’ve wired GitHub Issues, a Kanban workflow, repos, auto‑deploys, and a live Postgres DB.”
- Gap: “We’re moving work… and notice there’s no frontend ticket for archived items UI.”
- Ask EnderAI: “Create the missing frontend ticket for archived items UI.”
- Confirm: “Issue created and auto‑added to the board.”
- Execution: “As we close it, the board updates instantly.”
- Trust: “Flight Logs capture the full trail — requests, commands, outcomes.”
- Memory: “EnderAI reuses proven context from past tickets and captures new decisions as reusable memory.”
- Wrap: “This is a tighter ship loop: fewer misses, faster shipping, repeatable outcomes.”

## Required Artifacts
- Stable test data in DB (users/items)
- Kanban board configured to auto‑add new issues
- GitHub issue template for frontend features (optional)
- Flight Log updated during demo
- Example memory snippet to show “used” + “created”

## Risks + Mitigations
- Board automation delay → buffer in script with “refresh board” step.
- Rate limits/permissions → confirm tokens + device auth ahead of time.
- Deploy lag → pre‑warm deployments, or note “already deployed.”

## Callouts (On-screen)
- “Auto-added to Kanban”
- “Issue created from context”
- “Flight Log evidence captured”
- “Faster ship loop”
- “Memory used → Memory created → Repeatable outcomes”
